<article class="env-lemma" id="04IQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04IQ">Lemma <span data-tag="04IQ">7.30.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{F} = h_ U^\# $ for some object $U$ of $\mathcal{C}$. Then $j_\mathcal {F} : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})/\mathcal{F} \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/04GZ" data-tag="04GZ">7.30.1</a> agrees with the morphism of topoi $j_ U : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}/U) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ constructed in Section <a href="/tag/00XZ" data-tag="00XZ">7.25</a> via the identification $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}/U) = \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})/h_ U^\# $ of Lemma <a href="/tag/00Y1" data-tag="00Y1">7.25.4</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have seen in Lemma <a href="/tag/00Y1" data-tag="00Y1">7.25.4</a> that the composition $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}/U) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})/h_ U^\#  \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ is $j_{U!}$. The functor $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})/h_ U^\#  \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ is $j_{\mathcal{F}!}$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/04GZ" data-tag="04GZ">7.30.1</a>. Hence $j_{\mathcal{F}!} = j_{U!}$ via the identification. So $j_\mathcal {F}^{-1} = j_ U^{-1}$ (by adjointness) and so $j_{\mathcal{F}, *} = j_{U, *}$ (by adjointness again). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>